SkyCraft (fabric/)
------------------
The Fabric mod in fabric/ is derived from SkyCraft by chasmlol,
https://github.com/chasmlol/SkyCraft, MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 chasmlol:
its skeleton, the shared-memory link (protocol/skycraft_protocol.h, SkyLink),
the dig and wall code (SkyDig, DigWalls, DigMath, SkyDigClient and their mixins)
and the combat stand-ins. Full licence text: fabric/LICENSE-SkyCraft. Portalcraft
renamed the mod id (portalcraft), the shared-memory file (/dev/shm/Portalcraft_v1)
and removed SkyCraft's Discord application id, so it can run next to a real
SkyCraft. The Java package name dev.skycraft is kept from upstream.

Design reference
----------------
Immersive Portals (qouteall, Apache-2.0): the approach to carrying a player through
a portal, no code copied.

No game files from Valve or Mojang are included. Minecraft's textures are unpacked
at setup time from the user's own Minecraft 26.3 client jar (tools/extract_mc_assets.py)
into cache/minecraft-26.3, which is never committed.

fabric/src/main/java/dev/skycraft/world/SkyMovers.java (bridge #26)
  The movers' collision (an entity's box in a moving structure's own frame, a
  swept separating-axis test against its boxes, contact-point carry) is adapted
  from Create's ContraptionCollider / ContinuousOBBCollider,
  https://github.com/Creators-of-Create/Create (mc1.20.1/dev), Copyright (c)
  The Create Team / The Creators of Create, MIT License (code); full text in
  fabric/LICENSE-Create. No Create assets are used.
